# dev-pulse — example env file for local development.
#
# `resolve_secret` in crates/dev-pulse/src/main.rs maps `secret://NAME`
# handles in config.toml to env vars by upper-casing the name and
# replacing `/` with `_`. So `secret://github/pat` reads `GITHUB_PAT`,
# `secret://github/webhook_secret` reads `GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, and
# `secret://oauth/github_client_secret` reads `OAUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET`.
#
# Copy this file to `.env`, fill in the real values, then export
# before running `cargo run -p dev-pulse -- serve --config ...`:
#
#   set -a && . ./.env && set +a
#
# `.env` is gitignored; never commit real secrets.

# ----- fetcher GitHub PAT (SCOPE §15.1 stepping stone -----------------
# Classic or fine-grained PAT. Minimum scopes for read-only ingest:
#   repo:status, public_repo, read:org, read:user (classic), or the
#   fine-grained equivalents on the orgs you want to track.
GITHUB_PAT=

# ----- webhook HMAC secret (matches the value you paste into the ------
# GitHub App / webhook settings — see SCOPE §15.3 rotation notes).
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ----- operator OAuth (SCOPE §15.10) ----------------------------------
# Create a GitHub OAuth App with callback
#   {server.base_url}/auth/oauth/github/callback
# then paste its client secret here. The client_id lives in config.toml
# (not a secret).
OAUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
